```# AdaPlayground
AdaPlayground aims to provide a friendly environment to learn, experiment and test Ada code. It is a web-based tool developed by GNAT.

# Tools Used
- Visual Studio Code for Code Editing
- AdaCore's Ada Language Server for language support and debugging
- Anaconda and Jupyter Notebook for Data Analysis

# Features

## Code Editor
AdaPlayground offers a fully featured and syntax-highlighted code editor where you can write your Ada programs. The editor supports many of the features which are prevalent in Ada such as auto-completion, syntax highlighting, error detection, code refactorings etc.

## Code Execution and Debugging
AdaPlayground fully supports the execution and debugging of Ada code. It uses the GNU Ada compiler for code execution and provides easy-to-use debugging tools such as breakpoints and watches.

## Online Compiler
AdaPlayground includes the online compiler which can be used to compile the Ada code. The compiled code can run in the browser or it can be downloaded for local execution.

## Integration with Python, REST APIs and Node.js
AdaPlayground allows you to utilize Python, REST APIs and Node.js directly from within your Ada applications. 

## Data Analysis
AdaPlayground allows you to perform data analysis directly in your Ada programs using Anaconda and Jupyter Notebook. 

## Learn Ada with Advent of Code
AdaPlayground also includes a special feature called 'Advent of Code' which provides Ada solutions for the popular Advent of Code.

# Instruction Set 
In AdaPlayground, you can write programs in Ada, then visualize data, debug your code and even connect to a server to collect or manipulate data.

# Conclusion 
AdaPlayground is a great tool for anyone starting with Ada programming, as it provides all the elements needed to learn, experiment and make the most of this language.



























































































































































































































































































































